  "openQuestions": [
    "1. Collection pages: happenings-collection and blog-collection list items of the cms-happenings-blog-indiv collection. Recommend one instance per page with a Collection List in article-card-staggered_list (DynamoItem = article-card-staggered_item, bound to name, image, excerpt) instead of five static sections. Alternating left and right inside one list then needs an even-item rule (custom CSS .article-card-staggered_item:nth-child(even) or a per-item modifier); the plan as written places one card per section and uses is-right on the section, which matches the Figma file 1:1. Which does Stephen want?",
    "2. The list holds 1 card (collection pages) or 3 cards (neighborhood). A Webflow component cannot vary its child count without a slot. Use a slot on article-card-staggered_list if the MCP supports it (X01 probe), otherwise build the section as a component with the list unbound and insert items per instance, or skip the component and reuse the class family.",
    "3. Heading size differs per instance (heading-style-h4 on neighborhood, heading-style-h3 on culture). Webflow component props cannot swap a class. Options: two optional heading elements with visibility props (h4 and h3), or a Webflow component variant. Plan recommends two optional headings if variants are unavailable.",
    "4. Is the neighborhood header meant to stick while the cards scroll? Nothing in figma/animations/neighborhood.md says so; the plan leaves it static.",
    "5. Card images are Figma placeholders. Where do real images come from: CMS image field (collection pages) and a manual upload list for neighborhood dining cards?"
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "Added modifier is-right (not in the brief). The brief groups all 10 collection instances as base, but 04 and 06 place the card at x 816 (right) while 03, 05 and 07 place it at x 169 (left). One combo on the component covers it.",
    "Layout sits in container-large (80rem) per convention. The Figma frame is 1600 wide with content from x 42 to x 1560, so at 1440 and wider the right-aligned card ends at the container edge (about 2.75rem further in than Figma) and the is-tall intro starts at the container edge (about 2.5rem further in).",
    "text-style-eyebrow-caps and text-style-caps-caption-16 are applied as standalone classes carrying the full type values, not as combos on text-size-regular as figma/tokens.json proposes, so they can be reused on any element. K01 reconciles.",
    "Extra vertical space on is-tall lives on article-card-staggered_component.is-tall (padding 4rem top and bottom on top of padding-section-small) because a component instance cannot swap the shared padding-section-* utility.",
    "Card figure uses a #d9d9d9 fill with no variable as a placeholder until real images exist. Remove the fill once images are bound.",
    "Q025 build (2026-10-20): the component is the base single card only. The Data API has no slot props and an instance cannot switch the is-right or is-tall combos (same as Q016, Q017, Q020, Q021), so is-right, is-right with the culture header, and is-tall (3 cards) are plain reference sections on the build page.",
    "Q025 build: the headingStyle class prop is not possible; the header holds two h2 headings (heading-style-h4 and heading-style-h3, both text-weight-normal) bound to one Heading prop, toggled by Show Small Heading (on) and Show Large Heading (off).",
    "Q025 build: optional elements are boolean props bound to visibility (Show Header, Show Intro, Show Image, Show Eyebrow, Show Caption). Show Header defaults to off as the plan says, so the default instance shows the card only.",
    "Q025 build: the Image prop has no default (API limit) and Show Image defaults to off, so the grey #d9d9d9 figure fill shows. The reference sections hold no img element at all, for the same placeholder look.",
    "Q025 build: loading=\"lazy\" and alt=\"\" are left to the Image element defaults (alt inherits from the asset) instead of custom attributes.",
    "Q025 build: the is-tall text stack is ordered article-card-staggered_text is-tall text-size-medium, so the combo path is .article-card-staggered_text.is-tall.text-size-medium; the .article-card-staggered_text.is-tall rule still matches."
  ],
